{
  "about": "Shared test cases for live values (docs/2026-10-07-live-values.md). The designer (lib/live-value.ts), and later the firmware and the Android app, must agree on every case. `evaluate`: a live value's rules and a `value` that arrived (absent: nothing arrived; \"\" is an empty message that did); `applies` is the index of the rule that applies, or \"otherwise\", or \"noValueYet\". Rules are read top to bottom, the first that matches wins. `text`: what a live value reads as text - `liveValue` (its `format`, rules with text results, `otherwise`, `noValueYet`; a text result is a list of strings and {\"value\": true} for the value in its format) and a `value` as above; `decimal`/`thousands` default to . and '. `resolve`: a whole text with `{live:<id>}` references, the object's `liveValues`, and `values` keyed by `namespace:path`. `combined`: combined topics (`combinedTopics`, each a name, `mode` all or any, and conditions shaped like rules, their source a topic or another combined topic), the topic `values` that arrived, and what each combined topic reads: \"true\", \"false\", or null for no value yet; or `circular`, the chain a circular reference makes.",
